In Equation \eqref{eq:TempRainModel}, we considered a non-linear effect of temperature, following \cite{xu2020high}. The \texttt{ClimateType} variable is a binary variable which takes a value of `1' for the eastern section of the country, and takes `0' for the western section.  The country's western section has a pronounced dry and wet season, while the eastern part has relatively high rainfall all year round \citep{kintanar_climate,coronas1920climate}. Moreover, we considered an interaction effect between $\log$ rainfall and climate type. This is based on the results in \cite{cawiding2025disentangling}, which showed that the effect of rainfall varies for different regions of the country (see Section \ref{sec:literature}). The values $\widehat{\text{Temperature}}(B_i,t)$ and $\widehat{\text{Rain}}(B_i,t)$ are computed using Equation \eqref{eq:blockaverage}; see also Algorithms \ref{alg:plugin} and \ref{alg:resampling}.

