Let $W$ be a transitive inner model of $\ZFC$. A \textit{Cohen real} over $W$ is $x \in 2^\omega$ such that $x = \bigcup G$ for some $\mbbC$-generic filter over $W$. A \textit{random real} over $W$ is $x \in 2^\omega$ such that $\{ x \} = \bigcap H$ for some $\mbbB$-generic filter over $W$.
Recall that $x \in 2^\omega$ is a Cohen real over $W$ if and only if $x$ belongs to all Borel comeager sets coded in $W$.
Also, $x \in 2^\omega$ is a random real over $W$ if and only if $x$ belongs to all Borel conull sets coded in $W$.
We let $C^W$ and $R^W$ be the collections of all Cohen reals and random reals over $W$, respectively.

