   there is a pre-convergent map $\sigma$ from $( \omega^\omega , \leq^* )$ to $( \hat{\mcalM} , \supseteq )$.
   We define $f \colon \omega^\omega \rightarrow \hat{\mcalM}$ by $f(z)=\bigcup \sigma(z)$.
   It is easy to check that $f$ is a convergent map from $( \omega^\omega , \leq^* )$ to $( \hat{\mcalM} , \supseteq )$.
   By $(\star)$ we can take a set $S$ of ordinals and formula $\varphi$ such that
   \begin{center}
   $u\in f(v) \Leftrightarrow L[S][u][v]\models \varphi(S,u,v)$
   \end{center}
   for all $u,v\in\omega^\omega$.

