Let us describe the way we bound the probability $p_1$. Let us specify one of the two children of $u$ and call it {\it canonical}. For an even time step $\tau > 0$, let $\mathcal{Q}_1^*(\tau)$ denote the following event: there exists an extension $\tilde\xi_0$ of $\xi_0|_{V(T_u)}$ to the whole tree such that 
\begin{itemize}
\item $\tilde\xi_t(v)= \tilde\xi_0(v)=\xi$ for all even $t\leq\tau$; 
\item at least one of the children of $u$ has initial opinion $\xi$;
