 (k+1)k^{(h-d-1)} \cdot \mathbb{P}(\xi_0^* \in \mathcal{F}) = \Omega(1).
 \label{eq:sec_general_k_final}
 \end{equation}
 Due to~\eqref{eq:sec_general_k_pre_final}, we achieve~\eqref{eq:sec_general_k_final} by choosing small enough constant $c_-$ in the definition of $d$.
