\begin{theorem}\label{Theorem: alpha well-defined iff sigma extended}
    Let $A$ be an irreducible transition matrix for which the Exel-Laca algebra $\mathcal{O_A}$ is unital.  The following statements are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\alpha_0(\mathcal{G}_A) \subseteq \mathcal{D}_A$;
        %\item $\alpha_0$ is a function, i.e., we may write $\alpha_0 : \mathcal{G}_A \to \mathcal{D}_A$.%  (it is well-defined).
        \item There exists a $*$-endomorphism $\alpha$ on $\mathcal{D}_A$ which extends $\alpha_0$.
        \item $\sigma: \Sigma_A\sqcup F_A\to X_A$ is continuously extended in all $X_A$.
