\end{align*}
    where $\sigma_\mathcal{A}$ is the operator shift on $\Sigma_A(\mathcal{A})$. Now, we obtain $\mu(f)=\widehat{\mu}(f)=-\infty$. So we get what we wanted because the choice of $\mu$ was arbitrary.
