If the evidence for a closed universe is confirmed, it would necessitate a significant reevaluation of inflationary models, which typically predict an extremely flat universe due to the rapid exponential expansion during the inflationary epoch. Additionally, it would require revisiting our understanding of the global topology of the universe, which could have far-reaching consequences for fundamental physics and cosmological observations. 
