Let us discuss the energy-momentum tensor conservation. Taking the covariant divergence of both sides of (\ref{syneq}) yields:
\begin{equation}
\nabla_a \left[ R^{ab} - \frac{1}{2} g^{ab} R \right] 
+ \nabla_a (g^{ab} \Lambda) 
+ \lambda \nabla_a \left( {}^{(3)}R^{ab} - \frac{1}{2} g^{ab} {}^{(3)}R \right)
= 8\pi \nabla_a T^{ab}.
\end{equation}
Using the contracted Bianchi identity,
\begin{equation}
\nabla_a \left( R^{ab} - \frac{1}{2} g^{ab} R \right) = 0
\end{equation}
and the compatibility of the covariant derivative with the metric,
%\begin{equation}
$\nabla_a g^{ab} = 0$,
%\quad
%\Rightarrow \quad \nabla_a (g^{ab} \Lambda) = 0 \quad (\text{if } \Lambda = \text{const}),
%\end{equation}
we obtain the modified conservation equation:
\begin{equation}
\nabla_a T^{ab} = \frac{\lambda}{8\pi} \nabla_a \left( {}^{(3)}R^{ab} - \frac{1}{2} g^{ab} {}^{(3)}R \right).%=\frac{\lambda}{8\pi} \nabla_a{}^{(3)}R^{ab},
\end{equation}
In the case of ${}^{(3)}R=0$, which is slightly less general than $\int d^4 x \sqrt{-g}{}^{(3)}R=0$, we have
\begin{equation}
\nabla_a T^{ab} =\frac{\lambda}{8\pi} \nabla_a{}^{(3)}R^{ab}.
\end{equation}
In the synchronous gauge we have $\nabla_i=D_i$ for $i=1,2,3$. Then, because ${}^{(3)}R^{00}={}^{(3)}R^{i0}=0$ the equation simplifies to $\nabla_a T^{ab} =\frac{\lambda}{8\pi} D_a{}^{(3)}R^{ab}$. Using the Contracted Bianchi identities in 3 dimensions $ D_a{}^{(3)}R^{ab}=\frac{1}{2}  D_b{}^{(3)}R=0$ we get $\nabla_a T^{ab} =0$ - the standard energy-momentum tensor conservation.

