    Panels c-f show the instantons in phase space.
    (c) The type-II normal regime. (d) The type-I inverted regime. (e) The convex inverted regime. (f) The type-I normal regime.
    Note that there is no fundamental difference in the shapes of the convex and non-convex instantons in phase space. The key distinction lies between the normal and inverted regimes. }
