The flame is stabilized inside the combustion chamber using a swirl injector in a partially premixed mode. The cut section of the injector comprising of the swirler and central fuel injection tube, is provided in Fig. \ref{exp_line} (b). The air and fuel mixing occurred in the primary region before exiting through a diverging flare section having a diameter ($d_f$) of 32 mm. In this study, the divergence (or flare) angle of $\beta=60^\circ$ is considered and the combustion studies using other flare angles for pure methane is reported in \cite{Thiru2025_ECM}. The airflow enters the counter-rotating swirlers with a 6:4 split ratio, where 60\% of air passed through the primary vanes and 40\% air through the secondary vanes. The geometric swirl numbers of the primary and secondary swirlers are 1.5 and 0.78, respectively.

