From Fig. \ref{fig:DifferentCoatings} it is clear that the dependence of $\Phi_{exit}$ on the value of the critical energy of the walls is much stronger than $E^{3/2}_{lim}$. If the critical energy increases by 2 times, $\Phi_{exit}$ increases by 7.5 times, and not by 2.8 times. This fact indicates that when manufacturing the source, special attention should be paid to materials with high critical energy.

