To deepen our understanding of the bath properties, we study the spectrum of the Redfield Liouvillian and compare it to one of the Lindblad Liouvillian. Our results are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:Ohm_final}(a) for a cutoff frequency $\omega_c = 3/t$, corresponding to the evolution depicted in Fig.~\ref{fig:Ohm}(a). We observe that a small cutoff leads to the appearance of imaginary eigenvalues with small but non-zero real part %leading to dephasing
and causes the spectrum to deviate from the standard Liouvillian case. In addition, we compare in Fig.~\ref{fig:Ohm_final}(b) the Redfield Liouvillian spectrum for the two different cutoffs investigated in Figs.~\ref{fig:Ohm}(a)-(b). For the large cutoff $\omega_c = 10/t$ (violet dots) the spectra is already comparable to the Lindblad case and we observe the ORDLO.

