In order to solve the Redfield Equation~\ref{redfield}, we use the Bloch-Redfield master equation integrator provided by the Python package QuTiP~\cite{qutip}. Given the complexity of the numerical calculation related to the exponential growth of the Bloch-Redfield tensor, which slows down the numerical integrator, we present results of a maximum of $M=8$ sites.



