From the fibration obtained in Proposition~\ref{prop: ellipsoids}, we can recover the toric domains obtained in \cite{Ferreira2023GromovWO} as follows: First, we perform a transferring-the-cut operation by applying the matrix
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
1 & 0 \\
-1 & 1
\end{pmatrix}
\]
to the half-plane defined by $\mu \leq 0$. Then, we apply an appropriate $SL(2, \mathbb{Z})$ matrix to obtain the desired figure (see Figure~\ref{fig:convex_base_11c_2m}). One can perform an inverse nodal trade at the node with branch-cut emanating from the origin and a limit nodal slide at the second node. In the limit, we obtain a Lagrangian disk over the limiting point, which can be taken to be the cotangent fibre over one of the poles of the surface of revolution, agreeing with the case studied in \cite{Ferreira2023GromovWO}.



