Using the same group of ideas, we can also construct an almost toric fibration in the disk cotangent bundle $D^*D^2$ of the 2-dimensional disk $D^2$ of radius 1, also known as the Lagrangian bidisk. We adopt the same notation as in \cite{ramos2017symplectic} and define the Lagrangian bidisk as:
\[P_L=\{(p_1,p_2,q_1,q_2)\in \mathbb{R}^4~|~ p_1^2+p_2^2 \leq 1;~ q_1^2+q_2^2\leq 1 \},\]
with the symplectic form $\omega=\sum dp_j \wedge dq_j$.


\begin{theorem}\label{thm: lagbid}
There exists an almost toric fibration $f:(P_L,\omega)\to B_{P_L}$, where the region $B_{P_L}$ is bounded by the curve $(\mu,\mathcal{A}(\mu))$, see equation \eqref{eq: bound_lagbi}.
\end{theorem}

