\begin{definition}[Genetic Program]
A genetic program $\mathcal{P}$ is an element of  $ \mathcal{T} \times \mathcal{F}  \times \mathcal{E} $:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\mathcal{F}$ is a finite non-empty set of functions \\ 
\item $\mathcal{T}$ is a finite non-empty set of terminals \\ 
\item $\mathcal{E}$ is a finite non-empty set of edges \\ 
\end{itemize}
Let $\phi$: $\mathcal{P} \mapsto \Psi$ be a decode function which maps $\mathcal{P}$ to a phenotype $\Psi$	 
\label{definition_gpr}
\end{definition}


