\section{2-Periodic Friezes of Type $E$}
% ===============================================

Initial analysis, as in type $D_n$, shows that 2-periodic friezes of type $E_6$ and $E_8$ 
must actually be constant.
In the remaining case $E_7$, the same analysis shows which $\tau$-orbits must be constant,
so the general frieze will be as follows.

\begin{equation}\label{eq:E7frz}
\begin{tikzpicture}[friezeM, baseline=(bb.base)]
\pgfmathsetmacro{\frzTop}{3}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\frzBot}{-2}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\frzExtra}{0.7}
