Thus combining \eqref{reduction1}, \eqref{reduction2} we get, $\left(N(u),u_t\right)\leq \tilde{\eta}((Du_t,u_t)+\delta E(u,u_t)+b\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)$ 
   and  $b(s)= c_{\tilde{\eta}} \cdot s^{\frac{q+2}{7q+6}\left(1+\frac{16(q+1)}{5q+2}\right)}$ for some constant $c_{\tilde{\eta}}>0$\\
To conclude the above lemma we next claim that $\lim\Big\{s^{1-\frac{1}{\gamma}}.b(s)\Big\}
     =0$ as ${s\to \infty}$.\\
    Observe that for any $q>0$,\begin{align}
     &\lim_{s\to \infty}\Big\{s^{1-\frac{1}{\gamma}}.b(s)\Big\}
     =c_{\tilde{\eta}} \cdot \lim_{s\to \infty}\Big\{s^{1-\frac{2(q+1)}{q}}.s^{\frac{q+2}{7q+6}(1+\frac{16(q+1)}{5q+2})}\Big\} 
